{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778285663,"nonce":"CLVMrUeVAXtRhoxFlLr+atgqU6g=","title":"Refactor cross-timestep loss family: unified NthDifferenceLoss (or similar) instead of separate StateDerivativeLoss + OutputJerkLoss","message":"## Motivation\n\nCurrently `feedbax.loss` exposes two cross-timestep loss terms with overlapping mechanics:\n\n- `StateDerivativeLoss` (issue e8f3738, commit 380cbd1): order=1 cross-timestep, default leaf `state.net.hidden`. Penalises `‖h_t - h_{t-1}‖²`.\n- `OutputJerkLoss` (issue 7e1d257, commit 8439653): order=2 cross-timestep, default leaf `state.mechanics.effector.vel`. Penalises `‖x_{t+1} - 2·x_t + x_{t-1}‖²`.\n\nBoth are operationally an N-th finite difference of an arbitrary state leaf. The *name* and *default leaf* of each implies a specific use case but the mechanical operation is generic — `where` lets the user redirect to any leaf. This naming asymmetry is a design wart: a future user who wants a smoothness penalty on velocity, or a jerk penalty on activity, has to either rename mentally or pick the \"wrong\" class.\n\n## Proposed refactor\n\nIntroduce a unified family:\n- `NthDifferenceLoss(order: int, where: ..., time_axis: int = 1, ...)` — single class, parameterised by finite-difference order. order=1 reproduces StateDerivativeLoss; order=2 reproduces OutputJerkLoss; order=3 (third difference of position = jerk-from-position) is also accessible.\n- Keep StateDerivativeLoss and OutputJerkLoss as thin aliases / deprecations for backward compatibility (initial weight 0.0 in existing configs means deprecation is low-risk).\n\nThis pushes \"what does this loss do\" entirely into the (where, order) tuple supplied at construction, which is the correct factoring for a compositional loss menu.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The streaming-loss extension to support cross-timestep terms is tracked separately as `d67e303`. Both StateDerivativeLoss and OutputJerkLoss currently require `--no-streaming-loss`. The refactor here does not change that; it just unifies the API.\n\n## Cross-references\n\n- Surfaced from rlrmp work on the 2x2x2 baseline matrix (rlrmp issue efc4d68); will be cross-linked from rlrmp meta coord 1d9ae6f.\n- Sibling issues: e8f3738 (StateDerivativeLoss), 7e1d257 (OutputJerkLoss), d67e303 (streaming extension).\n\n## Status\n\nDeferred — current implementations are correct and shipped. Refactor when next touching this area of feedbax.","files":null}]}